  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">KFTC Expert Dispatch</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Backgrond: In 2008, at the request of the competition authorities of Vietnam and Indonesia, staff from the KFTC were dispatched to foreign competition authorities for approximately four weeks to conduct training for local competition authority staff. Since then, there has been a continuous demand, including requests for the dispatch of experts. Similar to the Internship Program, this initiative can serve as a channel for cooperation with foreign competition authorities.

 Objectives: By dispatching experts(current staff of the KFTC) with extensive experience in competition law enforcement to newly established competition authorities that lack such experience, we can provide practical assistance. Over a period of 2-4 weeks, these experts will closely communicate with the local competition authorities, offering advice on ongoing cases and upcoming amendments of new legislation. This will not only help the local authorities in enforcing competition law but also guide them to avoid making unfair decisions against our companies operating in those countries.

 Overview: After identifying the areas in which the recipient country`s competition authority wishes to receive training, we select the KFTC staff with significant experience in those fields. These staff members will closely communicate with local employees before their dispatch and conduct on-site training for about 2-4 weeks.</narrative>
  </description>
